{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Or a hunchback.</b> Related to the derivation of הרים גבנונים (hunchbacked mountains); the nun is a root letter and it is an adjective." "So too <b>dak</b> — it is as it sounds, being thin of short stature." "<b>A blemish in his eye.</b> Some say from the root of תבל (to perish), meaning destruction; others say from בלולה בשמן (mixed with oil), and the tav is added in both interpretations." "Also <b>garav</b> [scurvy] in the eye, according to the opinion of many, is so too." "<b>Yalafet.</b> Like the meaning of דבק (stuck), from the derivation of וילפת שמשון (Judges 16:29). Others say: עיות (distorted), from the derivation of ויחרד האיש וילפת (1 Samuel 28:21), and the yod is added like the yod of יצהר." "<b>Meruach.</b> An adjective, from the root רוח (wind/spirit)." "<b>Testicle.</b> The egg [i.e., testis]. And after he specified, he stated a general rule: כל איש אשר בו מום (any man who has a blemish in him)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:40.017510693Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}